{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1546016-gaolers-of-ialdabaoth-2e-fan-conversaion","id":1546016,"title":"Gaolers of Ialdabaoth - 2e Fan conversaion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-16T20:39:14-08:00","id":1546016,"title":"Gaolers of Ialdabaoth - 2e Fan conversaion","content":"<u><b>Gaolers of Ialdabaoth</b></u><br /> <i>The Wise Brethren</i><br /> <br /> Pages 82-91 of Grimoire of Grimoires for lore on the legacy and the associated grimoire.<br /> <br /> <b>Doctrine and Magic<br /> <br /> Parent Path:</b> Any<br /> <b>Parent Order:</b> Any<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spirit 2, Death 1 <i>or </i>Mind 1, 2 dots in Occult, one of the following addition skills at 2 dots or higher: Athletics, Larceny, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> <b>Initiation:</b> Discover the secrets of the Ialdabaoth Codex and then travel to the Temenos realm of the legacy. By studying the realm you can shape your Gnosis to the legacy.<br /> <b>Ruling Arcana:</b> Spirit<br /> <b>Yantras: </b>Chains (+1); Prisons (+1); The Ialdabaoth Codex (+3);<br /> <b>Oblations: </b>Studying the The Ialdabaoth Codex; Conducting interviews with mages who have been exposed to The Ialdabaoth Codex to make sure they haven't been corrupted; Imprisoning an Abyssal Manifestation in The Ialdabaoth Codex.<br /> <br /> <b>Attainments</b><br /> <br /> Each attainment listed below have two optional attainments, one gained from Death, and one gained from Mind. When joining the legacy, the mage must have Spirit 2 and then either Death 1 or Mind 1, which will determine the path they are on. Mages with Death specialize in dealing with the ghost mages of scelesti and ghosts that have been tainted by the abyss, while mind mages focus on the acamoth of the Astral Realms. A mage who studies both Death and Mind can choose which path to go down, but they are locked into that path, switching to the other path should be treated like creating a novel legacy attainment.<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment: Eyes of the Wise</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Prerequisites: Initiation</span><br /> The Wise Brethren learned first that they must be able to see the monsters they have chosen to face, and so their first attainment allows this. After an hour of meditation the mage can see into spiritual twilight as per \u201cExorcist's Eye\u201d (Spirit 1, MtAw 180). This attainment has advanced duration. For the purposes of this attainment, it also sees all non-specific ephemeral Abyssal manifestations.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Optional: Death 1</span><br /> If the mage is on the Death path of the legacy, this effect extends to Death twilight as if they were under the effects of \u201cSpeak with the Dead\u201d (Death 1, MtAw 128) with advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Optional: Mind 1</span><br /> If the mage is on the path of Mind this effect extends to Mind twilight, seeing any goetia in twilight, including any acamoth. This attainment has advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment: Compel Pneuma</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Prerequisites: Spirit 2, 2 dots in Death <i>or</i> 2 dots in Mind, 3 dots in Occult</span><br /> At their height there were many of the Wise Brethren working towards their mission, but only one Codex to bind the demons they faced to. At times, a mage found themself in a situation where they would need to travel long distances with an Abyssal monster stored away. This attainment allowed them to do so, similar to the spell \u201cSoul Jar\u201d (Death 2, MtAw 129), after an hour of ritual, the mage could bind an ephemeral entity into an object designed to hold and seal liquid. This effect has advanced duration. Mages on the path of Death could do this with ghosts as well, and mages on the path of Mind could use this attainment on goetia. The attainment has reach for instant casting and advanced duration, meaning the Gaoler must touch the entity they wish to imprison in the jar. To facilitate this need, instead of having optional attainments at this level, the Wise Brethren also learn the ability to strike ephemeral entities, as if under the effect of \u201cGossamer Touch\u201d (Spirit 2, MtAw 181) with reach for advanced duration. If they are on the path of Death this effect extends to ghosts, and the path of Mind extends this effect to goetia. This takes one hour of meditation to activate. The binding part of this attainment can be used against non-Abyssal ephemeral entities, but the Wise Brethren had a taboo against doing so.<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment: Pneumatic Armor</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Prerequisites: Spirit 3, The optional skill used to meet the requirements of initiation must be raised to 3 or a second option from the list must be raised to 2</span><br /> The Wise Brethren battle horrors from beyond, and must be prepared to defend themselves against the magic their enemies possess. This attainment activates after an hour of meditation, and functions like \u201cEphemeral Shield\u201d (Spirit 2, MtAw 181) with reach for advanced duration and to extend the protection to physical attacks from the creatures.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Optional: Death 3</span><br /> Mages on the path of Death further expand on this power to shield themselves against the magic of the dead, as if they were under the effects of \u201cGhost Shield\u201d (Death 2, MtAw 129) with reach for advanced duration. This optional attainment activates with the primary attainment and to extend the protection to physical attacks from the creatures.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Optional: Mind 3</span><br /> Mages on the path of Mind expand on this armor by extending its defenses to horrors born of the Inner Realms, as if they were under the effect of \u201cMental Shield\u201d (Mind 2, MTAw 160) with reach for advanced duration. This optional attainment activates with the primary attainment and to extend the protection to physical attacks from the creatures.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment: Plemoric Chains</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Prerequisites: Spirit 4, Death 4, <i>or</i> Mind 4, 4 dots in Occult</span><br /> While all demons of the Abyss must be bound and destroyed, not all need to be bound and destroyed immediately. Sometimes, the Wise Brethren found, it is best to use them, either forcing them to undo damage they have done, to be forced to give up information, or to simply sit still while they are bound to the Codex. This attainment facilitates that by acting as \u201cCommand Spirit\u201d (Spirit 2, MtAw 181) with reach for advanced duration, instant casting, and sensory range. If the mage has Mind 2 they may bind Astral creatures to the grimoire, and Death 2 allows them to bind ghosts. Like the rote, so long as they are bound to the Ialdabaoth Codex the attainment is lasting. This attainment only works on ephemeral Abyssal manifestations, or ephemeral creatures that have been tainted by the Abyss. It costs one mana to activate.<br /> <br /> In addition to the ability to bind their quarry to the Ialdabaoth Codex, the Wise Brethren would sometimes find themselves needing to do the unthinkable, ending the life of someone possessed by an entity before they could bind or destroy it. Because of this, no optional attainment was developed at this level, instead, the Gaolers learned to free those who had been possessed so they could continue their work without the cost of life. This attainment functions as \u201cBanishment\u201d (Spirit 4, MtAw 182) with reach for advanced duration. Mages on the path of Death could affect ghosts and mages on the path of Mind could affect goetia. Like with the previous attainment, this can be used on non Abyssal aligned entities, but there is a taboo against it.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment: Rend Pneuma</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Prerequisites: Spirit 5, Death 5 <i>or </i>Mind 5, The optional skill used to meet the requirements of initiation must be raised to 4 or a second option from the list must be raised to 3 or a third option must be raised to 2</span><br /> Those manifestations of the Abyss that can be destroyed should be, and this final attainment allows the Wise Brethren to act as executioners instead of jailers. With reach for instant casting and sensory range, this attainment replicates \u201cShadow Scream\u201d (Spirit 4, MtAw 183), dealing five lethal damage to the target. Like with the previous attainments, the Wise Brethren had a taboo against using this against entities that were not of the Abyss, but there is no requirement not to.<br /> <br /> Instead of an optional attainment, this attainment has a secondary effect of this attainment is the ability to turn the area around the mage into a universal bane, causing an area around the mage to function as a bane to any spirits, Abyssal manifestations, and either ghosts or goetia, depending on which path the mage is on. This attainment can be activated instantly, and has advanced duration and advanced scale.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Rotes</b></u><br /> Several rotes appeared in the 1e book that were never converted to seconds editon, so I've done so here<br /> <br /> <i>Deny the Spectral Panoply (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Practice: </b>Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Athletics, Larceny<br /> The unquiet dead that the Wise Brethren face frequently arm themselves with ephemeral weapons and tools to fight back against their would-be jailors. This spell was created with the purpose to destroy those tools when the mage cannot destroy the ghost.<br /> This spell reduces the durability of deathly ephemeral items by potency. If this reduces the durability to zero the object is destroyed.<br /> <br /> <i>Mortal Veil (Prime \u2022\u2022)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Practice: </b>Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Occult, Subterfuge, Survival<br /> While the Thunder-Perfect Brotherhood first started battling the manifestations sent to them by the Ialdabaoth Concord they quickly realized it was their Gnosis being detected by the creatures that were sent to slay them, so they developed this rote to hide themselves.<br /> The subjects of this spell appear as sleepers to any Abyssal manifestations that encounter them, provoking a clash of wills if the manifestation tries to see through the spell.<br /> <br /> <i>Pleromaic Chains (Spirit \u2022\u2022)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Practice: </b>Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 mana<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Rank<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Academics, Athletics, Occult<br /> When the Abyss manifests it can take on many forms, each corrosive to the fallen world in their own way. The Wise Brethren knew this to be the case, however they learned that not all things that crawl out of the Abyss can be destroyed. Qasfah and his followers were forced to ask the question, \u201cWhat is the response to that which cannot be destroyed?\u201d This rote was created as an answer to that question; bind it.<br /> The spell binds one ephemeral abyssal manifestation or one spirit that has been corrupted by the abyss to the pages of the Ialdabaoth Codex, the mage must have enough scale to include both the subject and the grimoire. All the information on the creature is encoded in the Pleromaic Outcasts, which includes its ban and bane, its motives, its powers, etc. No secret of the creature is kept hidden once the codex has it within its pages. This effect is lasting.<br /> <i>Add Death \u2022\u2022</i>: Ghosts that have been corrupted by the abyss can be bound by this spell.<br /> <i>Add Mind \u2022\u2022</i>: Goetia that have been corrupted by the abyss can be bound by this spell.<br /> <i>+1 Reach</i> By reaching with this spell the mage can bind abyssal creatures to things other than the grimoire, but the effect is no longer lasting.<br /> <br /> <i>Unwinding Fleshy Bonds (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 + Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Practice: </b>Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Athletics, Intimidation, Occult<br /> The founder of the Wise Brethren learned quickly that not all of the horrors of the Abyss were of the correct substance to be bound within the pages of his grimoire-prison. Those who took the form of living monstrosities could not be forced into the pages of the codex, so Qasfah created this rote to make their forms more susceptible to the magic of his legacy.<br /> The subject of this spell must be a living creature. Its body is changed, patterned into spiritual ephemera. This is not a spell that moves a living creature into spiritual twilight, they are wholly spiritual ephemera now. This is used by the Wise Brethren to transform Abyssal intrusions with a living body into a form that can be imprisoned into the Ialdabaoth Codex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 08-29-2025, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-16T20:41:57-08:00","id":1546017,"title":"","content":"Hello! This is one of my favorite legacies from 1e, and the Ialdabaoth Codex is my favorite grimiore from the Grimiore of Grimiores book, so I've decided to include it in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1516734-a-mage-the-awakening-chronicle-in-los-angeles-actual-play#post1516734\">my chonicle</a> and one of my players decided they wanted to join the legacy around it, so, I've written up the legacy as I like it, we'll see if they decide to follow it as is or turn it into their own.<br /> <br /> The only thing I really struggled with when it came to it was the final Mind and Death optional attainments, otherwise I like it quite a lot. Any ideas on that final attainment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-17T05:27:08-08:00","id":1546025,"title":"","content":"One of my favorite Legacies from 1ed, great origins, paired with a very powerful and dangerous Grimoire, which is extremely versatile for plot hooks. The initiation via a secret Temenos temple is very thematic. Glad to see a 2ed port.<br /> <br /> Maybe it would be worth getting the Reach effect on the Shieldings, protecting from attacks as well ? In thr case of the final Attainment, maybe a universal Bane might be helpful. It could be a Weaving, with Reach assigned to instant use, advanced scale and advanced duration.<br /> <br /> An entire area becomes solid to them, now physical objects can be used as an improvised weapon or binding. Combined with the Shielding with a Reach, it would make them do a Clash of Wills penalized by Rank and, even if they pass, they would take retaliatory damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-17-2024, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-17T12:36:41-08:00","id":1546041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1546016-gaolers-of-ialdabaoth-2e-fan-conversaion?p=1546025#post1546025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my favorite Legacies from 1ed, great origins, paired with a very powerful and dangerous Grimoire, which is extremely versatile for plot hooks. The initiation via a secret Temenos temple is very thematic. Glad to see a 2ed port.<br /> <br /> Maybe it would be worth getting the Reach effect on the Shieldings, protecting from attacks as well ? In thr case of the final Attainment, maybe a universal Bane might be helpful. It could be a Weaving, with Reach assigned to instant use, advanced scale and advanced duration.<br /> <br /> An entire area becomes solid to them, now physical objects can be used as an improvised weapon or binding. Combined with the Shielding with a Reach, it would make them do a Clash of Wills penalized by Rank and, even if they pass, they would take retaliatory damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like all of that a lot and made the changes, alook over of attainments 2, 3 and 5 please to make sure I didn't mess anything up moving them around, and tyvm for the insights!<br /> <br /> and I agree 100%, the everything about this chapter is so cool, I was pretty happy when one of my players said they were interested in this legacy when I mentioned it to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-17T13:50:33-08:00","id":1546049,"title":"","content":"Happy to help and looking forward to reading about your player's experience with it.<br /> <br /> I think the Reach effect of <i>Pleromaic Chains</i> is essentially acting like <i>Bind Spirit</i> with a mana cost, forcing the Posession Manifestation on a target spirit towards a given object. Perhaps it might require 2 Reach instead.<br /> <br /> A possible alternative would be to instead give them <i>Command Spirit</i> with Reach assigned to instant use, sensory range and advanced duration. With it they can command the Abyssal to cooperate, undo any damage, give them any information without lies or omission, even following them to the location of the Codex to be bound.<br /> <br /> I think that in the fifth Attainment, the universal Bane effect should be separate to the main one. Since it has advanced scale, I think it has 3 main ways to be used. The first is to make characters into a Bane, giving them a &quot;corrosive&quot; effect when hit and making them less likely to be grappled. The second is to use it on weapons, containers and even ropes, making it possible to improvise just about anything into a viable tool. The third use is to make the terrain hostile, forcing them to flee (possibly taking damage as they cannot phase through objects), stay contained, fight in difficult conditions and probably psych them out.<br /> <br /> The drawback is that you are making an area hostile to all ephemeral entities you can affect, including Familiars, inhabitants of the area and just about anyone in the Shadow, Underworld and/or Astral. So I believe being able to switch between the precision of multiple individual targets and the AoE version would be helpful in fine tuning how they hunt the Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-17-2024, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-17T16:59:51-08:00","id":1546055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1546016-gaolers-of-ialdabaoth-2e-fan-conversaion?p=1546049#post1546049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Reach effect of <i>Pleromaic Chains</i> is essentially acting like <i>Bind Spirit</i> with a mana cost, forcing the Posession Manifestation on a target spirit towards a given object. Perhaps it might require 2 Reach instead.<br /> <br /> A possible alternative would be to instead give them <i>Command Spirit</i> with Reach assigned to instant use, sensory range and advanced duration. With it they can command the Abyssal to cooperate, undo any damage, give them any information without lies or omission, even following them to the location of the Codex to be bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, and then just not have the Pleromaic Chains spell just remain as a spell instead of an attainment, that gives them more utility at the higher levels and does make the spell a useful rote forever, good idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1546016-gaolers-of-ialdabaoth-2e-fan-conversaion?p=1546049#post1546049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that in the fifth Attainment, the universal Bane effect should be separate to the main one. Since it has advanced scale, I think it has 3 main ways to be used. The first is to make characters into a Bane, giving them a &quot;corrosive&quot; effect when hit and making them less likely to be grappled. The second is to use it on weapons, containers and even ropes, making it possible to improvise just about anything into a viable tool. The third use is to make the terrain hostile, forcing them to flee (possibly taking damage as they cannot phase through objects), stay contained, fight in difficult conditions and probably psych them out.<br /> <br /> The drawback is that you are making an area hostile to all ephemeral entities you can affect, including Familiars, inhabitants of the area and just about anyone in the Shadow, Underworld and/or Astral. So I believe being able to switch between the precision of multiple individual targets and the AoE version would be helpful in fine tuning how they hunt the Abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>The intent is for them to be two seperate powers, without an optional attainment, I'll reword that to communicate it better.<br /> <br /> Will make these updates later, likely tomorrow!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-17T20:34:26-08:00","id":1546060,"title":"","content":"done, looks really good, thanks for always weighing in Kaiser! I do look forward to your input everytime at this point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}